{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/reversed"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every column’s sources and targets swapped, every entry negated (a vertex on both sides"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stays 0): Gallo et al.‘s symmetric image. An involution. O(1): the planes swap. A new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hypergraph: it carries none of this matrix’s attached maps."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/reversed","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reversed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"kind":"text","text":" { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"IncidenceMatrixModule","externalID":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V8reversedACvp","modules":[{"name":"IncidenceMatrixModule"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reversed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift#L593","fileName":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix.swift"},"title":"reversed","symbolKind":"property"},"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/reversed":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reversed","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:21IncidenceMatrixModule08OrientedaB0V"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Every column’s sources and targets swapped, every entry negated (a vertex on both sides","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stays 0): Gallo et al.‘s symmetric image. An involution. O(1): the planes swap. A new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hypergraph: it carries none of this matrix’s attached maps.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix\/reversed","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"reversed","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/reversed"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix":{"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","abstract":[{"text":"The oriented incidence matrix of a directed hypergraph: entry (v, p) is −1 when ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of column ","type":"text"},{"code":"p","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", +1 when it is a target, and 0 otherwise. Gallo, Longo, Pallottino and Nguyen"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1993) define a directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"type":"text","text":". It conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","type":"topic"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule":{"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule","title":"IncidenceMatrixModule","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule","role":"collection","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}